   "tag": "p×2",
   "landmarks": [
    "main",
    "section"
   ],
   "textLength": 546,
   "text": "In some countries, people have become infected with bird flu after close contact with infected birds or other animals. Outbreaks have been reported in wild birds, poultry (such as chickens or ducks), sea mammals and livestock (such as cows). Infections in humans are rare and linked to direct contact with infected animals or contaminated environments.\nThe risk of bird flu spreading in the community",
